IMPORT prelude

-- Singapore Convention on Mediation Act 2020 (Singapore) -- which mediated settlement agreements the Act reaches (ss 2, 3, with
-- articles 1 and 2 of the Convention in the Schedule), who may apply to record or invoke one (s 4), what the applicant must file
-- (s 6), the grounds on which the court may refuse (s 7), setting aside an order made in a party's absence (s 8), and parallel
-- proceedings (s 9). Section 5 (effect of recording) is quoted but its effect is not computed beyond the s 8 rule.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 1/4/2022), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/SCMA2020.txt. The revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including
-- 1 December 2021"; the latest amendment annotated is Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022 (s 5, "grant permission to record").
-- The ARRANGEMENT OF SECTIONS in the deposit is one number out of step with the body; the body's numbering is followed here.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0049 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario
-- has asked a sharper question yet. SCOPED to what a business holding a mediated settlement meets. Not encoded: Rules of Court
-- and regulations (ss 10, 11), the Convention's treaty machinery (articles 8 to 16 beyond the fact of a reservation), the
-- interpretation rules for regional organisations and non-unified States (articles 12, 13), and fees (none are in the Act).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Singapore Convention on Mediation Act 2020 -- enforcement`

DECLARE State IS ONE OF
    Singapore
    Malaysia
    Indonesia
    China
    India

§§ `2(1) -- mediation`

-- s 2(1): "mediation" means a process (whether called "mediation" or "conciliation" or any term of similar import) "(a) by which
-- the parties ... attempt to reach an amicable settlement of their dispute with the assistance of one or more third parties
-- (called in this Act the mediator); and (b) in which the mediator lacks the authority to impose a solution upon the parties".
-- "settlement agreement" means "an agreement resulting from mediation and concluded in writing by the parties to the mediation
-- to resolve a commercial dispute". s 2(2): in writing "if the contents ... are recorded in any form", including an electronic
-- communication "accessible to be useable for subsequent reference". "Commercial" is not defined.
GIVEN `assisted by a third party` IS A BOOLEAN, `the third party could impose a solution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the process is mediation` IF
    `assisted by a third party` AND (NOT `the third party could impose a solution`)

§§ `Schedule article 2(1) -- whose place of business counts`

-- Art 2(1)(a): if a party has more than one place of business, "the relevant place of business is that which has the closest
-- relationship to the dispute resolved by the settlement agreement"; (b) "If a party does not have a place of business,
-- reference is to be made to the party's habitual residence."
GIVEN `has a place of business` IS A BOOLEAN, `place of business closest to the dispute` IS A State, `habitual residence` IS A State
GIVETH A State
`the party's relevant State` MEANS
    IF `has a place of business` THEN `place of business closest to the dispute` ELSE `habitual residence`

§§ `3 and Schedule article 1 -- which settlements the Act reaches`

-- s 3(1): the Act applies to a settlement agreement which, "at the time of its conclusion, is international" within article 1,
-- paragraph 1(a) and (b), read with article 2, paragraph 1. Art 1(1): international if "(a) At least two parties ... have their
-- places of business in different States; or (b) The State in which the parties ... have their places of business is different
-- from either: (i) The State in which a substantial part of the obligations ... is performed; or (ii) The State with which the
-- subject matter ... is most closely connected."
-- s 3(2): the Act does not apply to (a) a settlement agreement in article 1, paragraph 2 or 3 -- art 1(2)(a) a consumer's dispute
-- "for personal, family or household purposes", (b) "family, inheritance or employment law"; art 1(3)(a) agreements approved by
-- a court or concluded in court proceedings AND enforceable as a judgment in that State, (b) agreements "recorded and enforceable
-- as an arbitral award" -- or (b) one covered by a reservation by Singapore under article 8 that is not withdrawn. The deposit
-- does not say whether Singapore has made any reservation; it is an input here.
-- Two parties are modelled. Their States are the relevant States under article 2(1).
DECLARE Settlement HAS
    `resulted from mediation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `recorded in some form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `resolves a commercial dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
    `first party's State` IS A State
    `second party's State` IS A State
    `State where a substantial part of the obligations is performed` IS A State
    `State most closely connected with the subject matter` IS A State
    `a consumer's personal, family or household dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
    `relates to family, inheritance or employment law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `approved by or concluded before a court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `enforceable as a judgment of that court's State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `recorded and enforceable as an arbitral award` IS A BOOLEAN
    `covered by an unwithdrawn Singapore reservation` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the settlement` IS A Settlement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement is a settlement agreement` IF
        `the settlement`'s `resulted from mediation`
    AND `the settlement`'s `recorded in some form`
    AND `the settlement`'s `resolves a commercial dispute`

GIVEN `the settlement` IS A Settlement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement is international` IF
        (NOT (`the settlement`'s `first party's State` EQUALS `the settlement`'s `second party's State`))
    OR  (NOT (`the settlement`'s `first party's State` EQUALS `the settlement`'s `State where a substantial part of the obligations is performed`))
    OR  (NOT (`the settlement`'s `first party's State` EQUALS `the settlement`'s `State most closely connected with the subject matter`))

GIVEN `the settlement` IS A Settlement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement is excluded` IF
        `the settlement`'s `a consumer's personal, family or household dispute`
    OR  `the settlement`'s `relates to family, inheritance or employment law`
    OR  (`the settlement`'s `approved by or concluded before a court` AND `the settlement`'s `enforceable as a judgment of that court's State`)
    OR  `the settlement`'s `recorded and enforceable as an arbitral award`
    OR  `the settlement`'s `covered by an unwithdrawn Singapore reservation`

-- s 2(1): "international settlement agreement" means a settlement agreement to which this Act applies under section 3.
GIVEN `the settlement` IS A Settlement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an international settlement agreement` IF
        `the agreement is a settlement agreement` `the settlement`
    AND `the agreement is international` `the settlement`
    AND (NOT (`the agreement is excluded` `the settlement`))

§§ `4 -- who may apply`

-- s 4(1): "a party to an international settlement agreement may -- (a) apply to the High Court to record the agreement as an order
-- of court" for enforcing it or invoking it to prove a matter already resolved; or (b) in proceedings in the High Court or the
-- Court of Appeal to which the party is a party and which involve a dispute the party claims was already resolved, apply to
-- invoke the agreement. s 2(1): "parties", in relation to a mediation, "does not include any mediator". s 4(2): the section
-- "does not limit or restrict any right or remedy ... that exists or may arise apart from this Act".
DECLARE Applicant IS ONE OF
    `a party to the agreement`
    `the mediator`
    `a stranger to the agreement`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant, `the settlement` IS A Settlement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply to record the agreement as an order of court` IF
        `the applicant` EQUALS `a party to the agreement`
    AND `it is an international settlement agreement` `the settlement`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant, `the settlement` IS A Settlement, `a party to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `claims the matter was already resolved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply to invoke the agreement in proceedings` IF
        `the applicant` EQUALS `a party to the agreement`
    AND `it is an international settlement agreement` `the settlement`
    AND `a party to the proceedings`
    AND `claims the matter was already resolved`

§§ `6 -- what the applicant must file`

-- s 6(1): the applicant "must provide" (a) the agreement "signed by the parties" or a certified copy; (b) evidence that it
-- resulted from mediation, "such as -- (i) the signature ... of the mediator ...; (ii) a document signed by the mediator ...
-- indicating that the mediation was carried out; (iii) an attestation by the institution that administered the mediation; or
-- (iv) in the absence of sub-paragraph (i), (ii) or (iii), any other evidence acceptable to the court".
-- s 6(4): if the agreement "is not in English", it "must be accompanied by a certified translation of it in the English
-- language". (Article 4(3) of the Convention says only that the authority "may request a translation".)
-- s 6(3): the court may require "any necessary document" to verify the Convention's requirements (not modelled).
DECLARE Filing HAS
    `signed agreement or certified copy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `mediator signed the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `mediator signed a document saying the mediation happened` IS A BOOLEAN
    `institution attestation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `other evidence the court accepts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `agreement is in English` IS A BOOLEAN
    `certified English translation` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the filing` IS A Filing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is evidence of mediation` IF
        `the filing`'s `mediator signed the agreement`
    OR  `the filing`'s `mediator signed a document saying the mediation happened`
    OR  `the filing`'s `institution attestation`
    OR  `the filing`'s `other evidence the court accepts`

GIVEN `the filing` IS A Filing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the filing meets section 6` IF
        `the filing`'s `signed agreement or certified copy`
    AND `there is evidence of mediation` `the filing`
    AND (`the filing`'s `agreement is in English` OR `the filing`'s `certified English translation`)

-- s 6(2): a signature requirement is met for an electronic communication if "(a) a method is used to identify the parties or the
-- mediator ... and to indicate the parties' or mediator's intention ...; and (b) the method used is either -- (i) as reliable as
-- is appropriate for the purpose ... in the light of all the circumstances, including any relevant agreement; or (ii) proven in
-- fact to have fulfilled the functions described in paragraph (a), by itself or together with further evidence".
GIVEN `identifies the signer and indicates intention` IS A BOOLEAN, `as reliable as appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proven in fact to have done so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an electronic signature counts` IF
    `identifies the signer and indicates intention` AND (`as reliable as appropriate` OR `proven in fact to have done so`)

§§ `7 -- grounds for refusing`

-- s 7(1): the court "may, at the request of the party (A) against whom the international settlement agreement is sought to be
-- enforced or invoked, refuse to grant the application if A furnishes proof of any of the grounds" in (2): (a) a party "was under
-- some incapacity"; (b) the agreement (i) "is null and void, inoperative or incapable of being performed" under its governing law,
-- (ii) "is not binding, or is not final, according to its terms", or (iii) "has been subsequently modified"; (c) the obligations
-- (i) "have been performed" or (ii) "are not clear or comprehensible"; (d) granting it would be contrary to the agreement's terms;
-- (e) "a serious breach by the mediator ... of the standards applicable", "without which breach A would not have entered into"
-- the agreement; (f) a failure by the mediator to disclose circumstances raising "justifiable doubts as to the mediator's
-- impartiality or independence" which "had a material impact or undue influence on a party, without which failure that party
-- would not have entered into" it.
-- s 7(3): the court "may also refuse" if (a) granting it "would be contrary to the public policy of Singapore" or (b) the subject
-- matter "is not capable of settlement by mediation under the law in force in Singapore". These need no request by A.
-- (Article 5(1) of the Convention says relief may be refused "only if" a ground is proved. Section 7(1) does not use "only".)
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `a party was under some incapacity`
    `the agreement is null and void`
    `the agreement is not binding or not final by its terms`
    `the agreement has been subsequently modified`
    `the obligations have been performed`
    `the obligations are not clear or comprehensible`
    `granting it is contrary to the agreement's terms`
    `serious mediator misconduct that induced the agreement`
    `serious mediator misconduct that made no difference`
    `undisclosed mediator conflict that induced the agreement`
    `undisclosed mediator conflict that made no difference`
    `the respondent simply regrets the bargain`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ground is in section 7(2)` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `serious mediator misconduct that made no difference` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `undisclosed mediator conflict that made no difference` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the respondent simply regrets the bargain` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground, `A requested refusal` IS A BOOLEAN, `A proved the ground` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `contrary to Singapore public policy` IS A BOOLEAN, `not capable of settlement by mediation in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may refuse the application` IF
        (`A requested refusal` AND `A proved the ground` AND `the ground is in section 7(2)` `the ground`)
    OR  `contrary to Singapore public policy`
    OR  `not capable of settlement by mediation in Singapore`

§§ `5 and 8 -- recording, and setting aside an order made in a party's absence`

-- s 5(1): the High Court "may ... grant permission to record" the agreement as an order of court "if the requirements of this Act
-- are complied with". (2): once recorded it "may be enforced in the same manner as a judgment" of the High Court and relied on by
-- the applicant "by way of defence, set-off or otherwise".
-- s 8: where an agreement "has been recorded as an order of court ... in the absence of the party against whom the order of court
-- is sought to be enforced or invoked, the High Court may, upon the application of that party, set aside the order of court on any
-- ground on which the High Court may refuse to grant the application". A party who was present has no s 8 route.
GIVEN `recorded in that party's absence` IS A BOOLEAN, `that party applied` IS A BOOLEAN, `a refusal ground is made out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the High Court may set the order aside` IF
    `recorded in that party's absence` AND `that party applied` AND `a refusal ground is made out`

§§ `9 -- parallel applications or claims`

-- s 9: if an application or claim relating to the agreement "has been made to a court of any State, any arbitral tribunal or any
-- other competent authority which may affect the grant", the court "may -- (a) if [it] considers it proper, adjourn the decision
-- on the application; and (b) on the request of a party, order the other party to give suitable security".
GIVEN `a parallel claim that may affect the grant` IS A BOOLEAN, `the court considers it proper` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may adjourn` IF
    `a parallel claim that may affect the grant` AND `the court considers it proper`

GIVEN `a parallel claim that may affect the grant` IS A BOOLEAN, `a party requested security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may order security` IF
    `a parallel claim that may affect the grant` AND `a party requested security`
